<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ private sector earnings up 0.6 pct in Nov qtr.</title>
<headline>NZ private sector earnings up 0.6 pct in Nov qtr.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following information from the November quarterly employment survey was released by Statistics New Zealand on Tuesday:</p>
<p>Ordinary time average hourly earnings, change from same period of previous year:</p>
<p>Total	     Nov 1996 yr     Aug 1996 yr   Nov 1995 yr</p>
<p>NZ$		  $16.20	    $16.08	  $15.65</p>
<p>Pct change	 3.5		 3.4	     3.0</p>
<p>Private sector  Nov 1996 yr     Aug 1996 yr   Nov 1995 yr</p>
<p>NZ$		  $15.51	    $15.41	  $14.94</p>
<p>Pct change	 3.8		 3.7	     3.3</p>
<p>Public sector   Nov 1996 yr     Aug 1996 yr   Nov 1995 yr</p>
<p>NZ$		  $18.33	    $18.06	  $17.70</p>
<p>Pct change	 3.6		 3.1	     3.3</p>
<p>Ordinary time average hourly earnings, percentage change from same period of previous quarter:</p>
<p>		     Nov 1996 qtr    Aug 1996 qtr  Nov 1995 qtr</p>
<p>Private sector   0.6 pct	   0.3 pct	 0.5 pct</p>
<p>Public sector    1.5 pct	   1.6 pct	 1.1 pct</p>
<p>Total		0.7 pct	   0.7 pct	 0.6 pct</p>
<p>Jobs filled:</p>
<p>			  Nov 1996	 Aug 1996	 Nov 1995</p>
<p>Full Time (million)  1.08	     1.08		 1.05</p>
<p>Part Time (million)  0.44	     0.43		 0.42</p>
<p>Total (million)	1.52	     1.51		 1.47</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
</text>
